don't spend money until you're making  money it's one of the hardest things to  do as an entrepreneur but one of the  most important lessons that you can take  because anybody can spend money if I  gave you a million dollars I'm sure you  can find a million different ways to  spend it but making money is the  challenge and I want to make sure that  you're still around  I love bootstrapping up businesses but I  want to make sure that if you are not  still around in a couple of years  because you've blown through all your  money then you're not gonna be there to  realize the opportunity that's ahead of  you now question came in from Shelly was  one of my readers who's selling  meatballs she's had got gourmet chicken  meatballs and she said if I'm gonna  launch with no money can and should I  get purchase orders from companies who  be interested in purchasing the  meatballs for their stores and  restaurants absolutely try to line up  the sales before we even make the  product as much as possible if you're  making your own little gourmet meatballs  then maybe you can make some in your  kitchen just as samples but you don't  want to go out and spend tons of money  on something and then not have it work  out the worst thing you can do is spend  all this money get lots of inventory and  then find out that the market doesn't  want it and that's a common mistake a  lot of entrepreneurs make they have a  great idea for a t-shirt line or food  product or whatever it is and so you go  out and if you're gonna get somebody to  manufacture it for you there's these  minimum orders so suddenly you're now  stuck with 10,000 t-shirts or frozen  chicken dinners or whatever it is  sitting in your garage and nobody wants  it that's what I want you to avoid so go  out and start making sales see people  want this get the purchase orders if  people are saying yeah this is great  then you can go out and spend the money  too I'll actually make them if all the  feedback you're getting is saying now  we're not interested then you've just  saved yourself tons of time effort and  dollars I'm not going down the wrong  path  with my first software business we made  that mistake where we invested tons of  time and energy into building this one  feature that turns out nobody cared  about we thought it was cool we thought  it'd be really helpful  my partners were in the field so they  should know what we're doing but nobody  really cared about this feature now  luckily we had enough that was still in  the software that people would buy it  but we wasted so much time going down  the wrong path and from that moment on  we started building only around our  customers and we've talked to our  customers and we said what would you  like in the next version and our  prospects what can we do to make this  better for you and we charge them to  make the product for them and then  rolled it out to everybody else and so  we only built new features in around  what we knew our customers were  interested in and that's the right way  to build a business and so I hope you  learn from that you know that lesson my  mistake of going down the wrong path you  don't want to invest tons of dollars  into something because you think it's a  great idea  get some justification from the market  get them to say yes go out and get those  purchase orders if you can get purchase  orders you can get financing you can get  the money you need to launch this thing  if you can't get purchase orders then  maybe you shouldn't do this business  maybe you should find another way to  stand another way to market another  product to sell if nobody wants it then  that's a good indicator for you as to  what you probably shouldn't do so a  great question good luck with it Shelly  so those of you watching if you agree  please give it a thumbs up below  everybody who's trying to bootstrap  their business give it a thumbs up I  love seeing those come in and you have a  question for your business please leave  in the comment section below I always  read those and look forward to seeing  what you have to ask I'll see you soon  you
 

